    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Presumably 8 fingers, since the sum is correct in base 8.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the unknown base. The digit 7 requires $x>7$. Using place value,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n(2x+7)+(3x+2)&=6x+1\\\\\n5x+9&=6x+1\\\\\n9&=x+1\\\\\n8&=x.\n\\end{align*}$$\nIn base 8, $27_8=23$, $32_8=26$ and $61_8=49$, so $23+26=49$. Presumably the aliens have 8 fingers.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
